["To create a Google Form with a multi-select dropdown (checkboxes) that shows unique values from Column A of your Google Sheet, you can use the following Google Apps Script code:

```javascript
function createFormWithUniqueCheckboxes() {
  const ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
  const sheet = ss.getActiveSheet();
  const values = sheet.getRange("A:A").getValues();

  // Extract unique non-empty values from Column A
  const uniqueValues = [...new Set(values.flat().filter(value => value !== ""))];

  // Create a new form
  const form = FormApp.create('Form with Unique Checkbox Options');

  // Add a checkbox item with unique values
  const checkboxItem = form.addCheckboxItem();
  checkboxItem.setTitle('Select options');
  checkboxItem.setChoices(uniqueValues.map(value => checkboxItem.createChoice(value)));

  // Log the form URL
  Logger.log('Form URL: ' + form.getEditUrl());
}
```

### How it works:
- It reads all values from Column A.
- Filters out empty cells and duplicates to get unique values.
- Creates a new Google Form.
- Adds a checkbox question with the unique values as options.
- Logs the form edit URL so you can open and customize it further if needed.

Run this script from your Google Sheets Apps Script editor, authorize it if prompted, and check the logs to get the form URL.", ""]

