{"role": "assistant", "content": "To display unique values from a Google Sheet's Column A in a dropdown within an HTML page using Google Apps Script, you'll need to set up a web app. The following steps guide you through creating a simple web application that reads unique values from Column A and displays them in a multi-select dropdown.

### Step 1: Prepare the Google Apps Script

1. **Open Google Apps Script**: Go to your Google Sheet, click on `Extensions > Apps Script`.

2. **Clear any existing code** and paste the new script:

```javascript
function doGet() {
  return HtmlService.createHtmlOutputFromFile('Index');
}

function getUniqueValues() {
  const ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
  const sheet = ss.getActiveSheet();
  const dataRange = sheet.getRange("A1:A" + sheet.getLastRow()).getValues();

  let flatValues = [].concat(...dataRange).filter(String); // Flatten and filter empty strings
  let uniqueValues = [...new Set(flatValues)]; // Get unique values

  return uniqueValues; // Return an array of unique values
}
```

- The `doGet()` function serves the HTML file ('Index.html' in this case) when you access the web app URL.
- The `getUniqueValues()` function fetches unique values from Column A and returns them.

3. **Create the HTML file**: Click on `File > New > Html file`, name it 'Index', and replace any existing code with the following:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Dropdown from Sheet</title>
    <script>
      // Immediately-invoked function to load unique values for dropdown upon page load
      (function() {
        google.script.run.withSuccessHandler(function(values) {
          const selectElement = document.getElementById('unique-values-dropdown');
          values.forEach(value => {
            const option = document.createElement('option');
            option.text = value;
            option.value = value;
            selectElement.add(option);
          });
        }).getUniqueValues();
      })();
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h3>Select a Value:</h3>
    <select id="unique-values-dropdown" multiple style="width: 200px; height: 150px;">
      <!-- Options will be added here by the script above -->
    </select>
  </body>
</html>
```

This HTML contains a `<select>` element configured for multiple selections and uses an immediately-invoked function expression (IIFE) to fetch unique values from the server-side `getUniqueValues` function upon page load.

### Step 2: Deploy as Web App

1. **Save and Name Your Project**: Give your project a name if you haven't already.

2. **Deploy**: Click on `Deploy` > `New deployment`.
   - Click on `Select type` > `Web app`.
   - Enter a description for your deployment.
   - Under `Execute as`, select `Me`.
   - Under `Who has access`, choose who you want to have access to the web app (e.g., `Anyone`).
   - Click `Deploy`.

3. **Authorize and Grant Permissions**: You might need to authorize the script and grant it permission to access your Google Sheet data.

4. **Access the Web App**: Once deployed, you'll get a URL to your web app. Open the URL in your browser to see your dropdown with unique values from your sheet.

This setup provides a basic example of how to display unique values from a Google Sheet in a dropdown on an HTML page using Google Apps Script. Remember, every time you make changes to your script or HTML file, you may need to create a new deployment to reflect those changes."}
